# =====================================================================================
# GWIscan species manifest — MULTI-SPECIES runs
# =====================================================================================
# Copy this file to  config/species.tsv  to enable multi-species mode, then run
# gwiscan as usual. Every species below is processed in the same run.
#
# One row per species. TAB-separated. Whole-line '#' comments and blank lines are
# ignored (put each comment on its own line beginning with '#').
#
# Each species writes into its own final_results/<Prefix>/ and intermediate/<Prefix>/.
# The prefix also leads the systematic domain ids (Ath gives AthGNA001.1).
# Use SPECIES_PARALLEL to set how many species run at once.
#
# COLUMNS
#   Prefix        Short species label. Used verbatim in output paths and domain ids.
#                 Required and unique.
#
#   Proteome      Protein FASTA for that species, one protein per gene. Paths are
#                 relative to the project directory, or absolute. Required.
#
#   Annotation    Optional. The representative GTF/GFF3 the proteome came from, that
#                 is, the same one-transcript-per-gene set. Gives every member its
#                 chromosome, start, end, and strand. Leave the cell empty for a
#                 species whose annotation you do not have; that species is still
#                 analysed, only without chromosomal coordinates.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Prefix	Proteome	Annotation
Ath	genomes/Athaliana.fasta	genomes/Athaliana.gtf
Gma	genomes/Gmax.fasta	genomes/Gmax.gtf
